{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/39190-descendents-of-scions","id":39190,"title":"Descendents of Scions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-29T23:33:27-08:00","id":39190,"title":"Descendents of Scions","content":"I played the demo to the latest Redemption Cemetary game: Bitter Frost. In it, you play a woman who's the descendant of Sheena, a mortal woman, and Kahouti, the Owl Spirit. But the jealous Spirit of Cold seeks to erase your family lineage to spite Kahouti. And so, with on owl feather relic that makes items grow, you seek to save your ancestors, and with them, your existence. <br /> <br /> I set that up because, as the title to this thread states, I wonder if a player can have a Scion who's divine relative is further apart like grandparent or great-grandparent. How far in generation can a Scion be before the ichor is strained beyond worth? Can a player play a descendant of a divine bloodline and still be called a Scion?<br /> <br /> I hope that OP can make rules for this variation if it's possible in the Scion universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T23:36:28-08:00","id":39193,"title":"","content":"In First Edition, you could be the grand-child of a God before the ichor thinned too much,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T03:35:21-08:00","id":39288,"title":"","content":"Assuming your player's story was compelling, I'd let them go back a few generations. Don't let the game limit your stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T23:10:28-08:00","id":39816,"title":"","content":"As far as I understand it and mortal plus a scion equals a mortal. A demigod plus a mortal equals a scion of the demigod's divine parent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T05:52:21-08:00","id":39921,"title":"","content":"To clarify: <br /> \u2022 Mortal + Hero = Mortal<br /> \u2022 Mortal + (Demigod or God) = Scion of most recent Legend 12 ancestor.<br /> <br /> That is, it`s not a case of the Ichor weakening from generation to generation; it\u2019s a case of needing to strengthen the Ichor within oneself to the point that it can be passed on to one\u2019s children. You could be the great-great-great-great-grandson of Zeus as still be a Scion of Zeus, as long as all of your ancestors between you and Zeus achieved Demigod status before conceiving the next in line. <br /> <br /> Of course, it\u2019s largely a moot point in the default setting as I understand it, because Scions are only now returning to the world after a long absence. Second-generation Scions are probably children at this point, and third-generation Scions are exceedingly rare. And unless there\u2019s a way for Scions to attain Hero status without a Visitation, there were no long lineages of Scions \u201cholding down the fort\u201d while the Gods were away: heck, without Visitations, the last generation of \u201cScions\u201d were probably indistinguishable from ordinary mortals for all practical purposes; and the last Heroes in the World were Heroes when the Gods departed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T06:31:38-08:00","id":39937,"title":"","content":"I understood it otherwise. As long as the Scion is not God yet, his children will be Scions of his grandparent, hero or demigod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T06:12:27-08:00","id":40478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/39190-descendents-of-scions?p=39921#post39921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And unless there\u2019s a way for Scions to attain Hero status without a Visitation, there were no long lineages of Scions \u201cholding down the fort\u201d while the Gods were away</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Celestial Bureaucracy section of the Companion did have a little section on the Xian, which are a kind of 'Hero-lite' that's doable by self-awakening. But they never cross the threshold to Demigod, so they can't maintain true scion generations... except for the weird part about becoming minor Shen after dying. That puts them in a weird spot, so... maybe?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}